## Compatibility correction

The unified gate originally crashed because legacy Cypress EO and Elemi EO profiles store qualitative text in `character`, while three scorer paths assumed a numeric mapping. `engine/optimizer/scoring.py` now treats non-mapping character data as uncalibrated: it does not crash and does not fabricate radar values. Numeric profile dimensions for other materials remain unchanged.

Regression coverage is included in `tests/test_cypres_de_verre_formula.py` for both the luxury screen and the complete formula score.

## Pre-existing baseline exclusions

Before CYP-01 implementation, a clean focused baseline produced `102 passed, 4 failed`. The four failures were pre-existing: three stale stock-strength expectations and one separate profile-shape crash in the chemical-life-graph path. CYP-01 does not rewrite those stock expectations and does not claim the unrelated chemical-life-graph defect is fixed.

A broader selected verification batch after implementation produced `85 passed, 1 failed`. The remaining failure is `test_formula_release_gate_cli_accepts_commercial_trial_and_scaling_target`, where an unrelated temporary fougère formula fails its generated-artifact `analysis_input_hash` binding after the test rewrites that temporary file.

An unfiltered repository-wide `pytest -q` snapshot stopped during collection with 21 pre-existing environment/repository errors before executing the suite. The blockers include missing optional backend packages (`pytest_asyncio`, SQLAlchemy, and Alembic), archived recovery trees being collected as live test roots, and complexity tests importing missing base-commit symbols such as `FormulaDoseReceipt`. This receipt does not misrepresent that collection failure as a green full suite.

